# Loaded by Vite ONLY for `vite build --mode mobile` (see package.json "build:mobile",
# used by "cap:sync"). Not read by `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, or any Netlify web
# build — those keep using their own env sources unchanged.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the Capacitor webview loads the app from its own local origin
# (https://localhost on Android, capacitor://localhost on iOS — see capacitor.config.ts),
# never from calmbeach.gr. A relative proxy base like the web build's "/api/forecast"
# would resolve against that local origin and 404 — there is no server there. Mobile
# needs the ABSOLUTE production URL instead.
#
# Not a secret: this is a public URL, safe to commit. If this file is ever missing,
# `vite build --mode mobile` still runs (Vite just finds no override), so
# VITE_FORECAST_PROXY_BASE ends up unset — and Batch 1's fail-closed logic in
# services/forecast/openMeteoProvider.ts then refuses to fall back to calling
# Open-Meteo directly (DEV is always false in a `vite build`), so a missing/broken
# value here fails closed rather than silently shipping a direct vendor call.
VITE_FORECAST_PROXY_BASE=https://calmbeach.gr/api/forecast
